--- stdout ---
Usage: /home/developer/console/.ci/scripts/ci/derive-image-tag.sh [OPTIONS]

Derive Docker image tag from Git ref or explicit input.

Options:
  --version TAG      Use explicit version tag
  --github-output    Write 'tag=VALUE' to GITHUB_OUTPUT
  --env-file         Write TAG, WEB_TAG, RENET_TAG to GITHUB_ENV
  -h, --help         Show this help message

Auto-derivation (when --version not provided):
  - Git tag (e.g., v1.2.3)  → uses tag name
  - Branch (e.g., main)     → uses version from package.json

Examples:
  /home/developer/console/.ci/scripts/ci/derive-image-tag.sh                              # Auto-derive, output to stdout
  /home/developer/console/.ci/scripts/ci/derive-image-tag.sh --version v1.2.3             # Explicit: v1.2.3
  /home/developer/console/.ci/scripts/ci/derive-image-tag.sh --env-file                   # Auto-derive, set GITHUB_ENV vars
  /home/developer/console/.ci/scripts/ci/derive-image-tag.sh --version latest --env-file  # Explicit with env export
